analysisWe need to produce assert statement for the comment in pop() method.

Comment: 
// @@@ If the list is initially not empty, then the result is either null and the first element was null before the operation, or the result is equal to the first element before the operation.

Interpretation: The method pop() returns removeFirst(). So the specification: If the list is initially not empty (i.e., \old(!this.isEmpty())), then the result (\result) satisfies: either (\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) OR (\result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))). Actually need to consider equality: For objects, we can use \result == null etc. Should we use .equals? In earlier examples they used .equals for query, but for generic E they may use .equals. Use \result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null OR \result.equals(\old(this.getFirst())) . However need to ensure result not null case: if result not null then equals old first. Could also write: (\old(!this.isEmpty())) => (\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) || (\result != null && \result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))). But the comment says "either null and the first element was null before the operation, or the result is equal to the first element before the operation." So we can express as: \old(!this.isEmpty()) => (\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) || (\result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))). Need to handle null equality: if old first null, result null case covered. If old first not null, then result equals old first.

Thus final assert: 
assert \old(!this.isEmpty()) => (\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) || (\result.equals(\old(this.getFirst())));

Make sure parentheses correct with => lower priority. So we need parentheses around RHS maybe: \old(!this.isEmpty()) => ((\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) || (\result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))));

Return final code block.

assistantfinal<code>assert \old(!this.isEmpty()) => ((\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) || (\result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))));</code>
